    "durationMs": 175222,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully verified against every requirement.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `cmd/server/main.go` — reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (no hard-coded credentials), retries until Postgres accepts connections, applies migrations, serves on `0.0.0.0:8000`, with graceful shutdown\n- `internal/api` — chi v5.2.1 router with `POST /links`, `GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}`; validation (absolute http/https URL with host, `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$` codes, malformed-JSON checks) and JSON error bodies for 404/409/422\n- `internal/store` — pgx v5 (via `database/sql` stdlib driver) persistence: atomic single-statement `UPDATE ... clicks + 1 RETURNING url` for redirects, unique-violation detection for 409 vs. generated-code retry with crypto/rand codes\n- `internal/migrate` — golang-migrate v4 with embedded SQL migrations (`links` table with unique `code`, BIGSERIAL ordering for list)\n- `start.sh` (executable) — builds and serves in the foreground; `README.md` documents startup\n\n**Verified by live HTTP tests**: 201 creation with unchanged URL and `clicks: 0` (both generated and custom codes), 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 for malformed JSON / missing url / relative url / ftp url / no-host url / short, long, bad-char, and empty codes, 302 + correct `Location` with clicks incrementing exactly once per request, 404 JSON for unknown codes on both GET routes, ascending list with `total`, and a full restart test confirming links and click counts persist in PostgreSQL. The test server was stopped afterward, so port 8000 is free for the grader's `sh start.sh`."
  }
